# =====================================================================
# CSO FUNNEL · Akshay Paliwal · Fractional Sales Co-Founder
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill every value. A comment above each
# var says what it is, where in the dashboard to find it, and what breaks
# without it.
#
# VERIFIED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: every var below is read somewhere in app/,
# lib/ or components/, and every process.env reference in the code has a
# var here. Nothing aspirational.
#
# NOT HERE, AND DELIBERATELY SO (Atul's scope call for this build):
#   · NO GA4. No NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID, no GA4_API_SECRET. There is no Google
#     Analytics on this project at all: no base tag, no browser events, no
#     Measurement Protocol purchase from the webhook.
#   · NO PABBLY. No PABBLY_WEBHOOK_URL. There is no fulfilment hand-off, so
#     nothing in this codebase tells an automation that a sale happened.
#     The webhook's only remaining job is Meta's Purchase.
# =====================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- SITE ---

# The live origin, with the scheme and no trailing slash.
# e.g. https://akshaypaliwal.com
#
# Read by lib/checkout-config.ts. It is the fallback event_source_url sent
# to Meta (reduced to its origin server-side), so leaving it blank quietly
# attributes live events to a placeholder host that nobody owns.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# The price in RUPEES, as a plain number. 197 for this offer.
#
# THE SINGLE SOURCE. lib/offer.ts turns it into every figure the buyer sees or
# is charged: the price on every button and in the refund sentence under them
# (cta.label and cta.note in app/_landing/content.ts, plus site.price), the
# figure reprinted on the checkout, the booking page, the thank-you and the
# legal pages, the paise amount the Razorpay order is created for, and the
# `value` on every Meta event.
#
# Nothing downstream types the number by hand, so changing it here changes all
# of them at once. That is the point: a button promising one price while
# Razorpay charges another is invisible until a buyer hits it.
#
# The guard is on a POSITIVE NUMBER, not on null: an empty value gives
# Number('') === 0, and without the guard that is a page advertising ₹0 and
# an order for zero paise with nothing throwing. Left blank it falls back to
# 197, which is what the copy source states.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICE_RUPEES=197

# NOTE: there is no booking env var. The payment lands on /book-a-call, the
# Cal embed is a constant at the top of that page (a NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is
# inlined at build time, so it would need a rebuild to change either way), and
# Cal hands the buyer to /thank-you once a slot is taken.


# ------------------------------------------------------------ RAZORPAY ---

# Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys.
# The key id is publishable by design (it is handed to the browser to open
# the payment sheet). The secret is not: it is server-only and must never be
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Without the pair, /api/razorpay/create-order returns 503 and the checkout
# says "Payments are not switched on yet" rather than failing silently.
#
# The key id also decides test versus live mode: lib/checkout-config.ts reads
# the rzp_test_ / rzp_live_ prefix rather than a separate flag, so the two
# cannot drift apart when someone swaps keys.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# ⚠️ A DIFFERENT VALUE FROM THE API KEYS. This one comes from
# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks, and it is the secret you type in when you
# register the webhook, not anything on the API Keys page.
#
# app/api/razorpay/webhook/route.ts verifies every call's HMAC against it and
# returns 500 when it is missing. Without it, Meta's Purchase never fires:
# no Purchase means no conversion data, and no conversion data means the ad
# account is optimising against nothing.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- META ---

# Events Manager → Data Sources → your dataset. The same numeric id goes in
# both: the NEXT_PUBLIC_ copy is inlined into the browser for the pixel base
# code, the bare one is read server-side by the CAPI routes. They are the
# same value and must stay identical.
#
# Without NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID no pixel and no PageView. Without
# META_PIXEL_ID the server events skip quietly, which means ViewContent,
# AddToCart, InitiateCheckout and Purchase all silently do nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
META_PIXEL_ID=

# Events Manager → your dataset → Settings → Conversions API →
# Generate access token. A long-lived system-user token, server-only.
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ⚠️ REMOVE BEFORE LAUNCH. Events Manager → Test Events gives a code like
# TEST12345. Events sent with it appear in Test Events and DO NOT COUNT
# toward optimisation, so leaving it set after go-live means a live funnel
# reporting nothing usable.
#
# lib/checkout-config.ts also treats a set test code as test mode.
META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE=


# ------------------------------------------------------------- CLARITY ---

# clarity.microsoft.com → your project → Setup. The short project id from
# the tag, e.g. abcd1234ef.
#
# This is the WHOLE analytics layer on this project. Read by
# components/Clarity.tsx, which renders nothing when it is missing, so an
# unfilled value leaves no broken script tag behind.
#
# Check the masking setting in the Clarity project itself: the privacy policy
# on this site states that keystrokes in form fields are masked, and this
# checkout collects a name, an email and a phone number.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=


# =====================================================================
